1. Ingestion Layer
PDFs uploaded to Object Storage (S3 / GCS / Azure Blob)
Metadata stored:
doc_id
source
upload_time
checksum (SHA-256)
➡️ Enables deduplication & retries

2. Orchestration & Scaling
Use workflow orchestrator
Airflow / Temporal / Step Functions
Batch PDFs into micro-batches (e.g., 100–200 docs)
Parallel workers for:
Text extraction
Chunking
Embedding
✔ Handles 10k/day without overloading downstream systems

3. PDF Processing
Extract text using:
PDFPlumber / Tika / OCR (fallback)
Normalize text:
Remove headers/footers
Fix encoding
Chunk text (semantic or token-based)

4. Deduplication Strategy
Two layers of deduplication:
A. Document-level
Hash full PDF content
If hash already exists → skip ingestion
B. Chunk-level
Hash normalized chunk text
Prevent duplicate embeddings across documents
➡️ Saves storage + embedding cost

5. Embedding & Indexing
Generate embeddings (OpenAI / HF / Cohere)
Store in:
Vector DB (Pinecone / Weaviate / FAISS)
Store raw text + metadata in:
SQL / NoSQL store

6. Failure Handling
Failures are expected — design for them
Idempotent pipeline stages
Retry with exponential backoff
Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) for:
Corrupt PDFs
OCR failures
Persist processing state:
INGESTED → PROCESSED → EMBEDDED → INDEXED
➡️ Pipeline resumes from last successful step

7. Monitoring & Observability
Metrics:
PDFs/hour
Failure rate
Duplicate rate
Logs per document ID
Alerts if SLA breached
